All 10 failing tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the 9 bugs fixed across the 3 modules:

**`src/auth.py`** (2 bugs)
- `has_permission`: compared with `in` (case-sensitive) → changed to lowercase comparison
- `is_admin_or_owner`: used `and` instead of `or` → owner *or* admin should grant access

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 bugs)
- Mutable default arg `{}` → all `Inventory()` instances shared state → changed to `None` with fresh dict in body
- `add` used `= qty` instead of `+= qty` → values were overwritten, not accumulated
- `reserve` used `>=` instead of `>` → reserving exactly the available quantity raised `OutOfStock`
- `release` didn't validate against going negative → releasing more than reserved would silently underflow

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 bugs)
- `slugify` didn't lowercase → added `.lower()` on iteration
- `slugify.replace("--", "-")` only collapsed pairs, not longer runs → replaced with `re.sub(r"-+", "-")`
- `truncate` appended suffix without reserving `len(suffix)` from `max_len` → changed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`
